# BASELINE.manifest — what the #589 integration suite EXPECTS of every test in
# this directory (#1101, accepted by the owner 2026-09-21, umbrella #1205).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. The suite used to demand an all-green run. Main is not all
# green and has not been for months, so a red suite said nothing about the change
# under test and the honest move — running it — was indistinguishable from the
# dishonest one. This file is the accepted baseline as DATA: 74 tests that passed
# on a clean main against the fleet device, and 11 that did not, each with a named
# cause and the issue that owns it. A reader can tell "known red, tracked in
# #1200" from "nobody knows", because the second thing cannot exist here.
#
# Evidence: test-history/integration-baseline/20260920T155254Z/report.md (the run,
# the device, the cause triage) plus 127acad (#1203), which moved 7 of that run's
# reds to green by fixing the runner's own wiring.
#
# WHAT THE SUITE DOES WITH IT (scripts/lib/integration-manifest.sh):
#   expect      fails  -> the suite FAILS. That is the whole point.
#   known-red   fails  -> reported, not fatal.
#   known-red   PASSES -> the suite FAILS. Move it to `expect` and update the
#                         `accepted` tally, citing the run that proves it. A test
#                         that quietly recovered but stays excused is how this
#                         list rots back into "22 failures, nobody knows why".
#   on disk, in neither list -> the suite FAILS, and fast gate 0 fails first.
#
# IF YOU ADD AN INTEGRATION TEST you must add a line here and bump `accepted`.
# scripts/test-integration-wiring.sh (fast gate 0, no emulator) fails otherwise.
# A new test goes in `expect` unless you can name the issue that owns its red.
#
# FORMAT — `|`-separated fields, `#` starts a comment, blank lines ignored:
#   accepted  | <baseline run id>      | expect=N | known-red=N | elsewhere=N
#   expect    | <file>_test.dart
#   known-red | <file>_test.dart       | #issue   | one-line reason
#   elsewhere | <file>_test.dart       | <the runner that owns it>
# No field may contain a `|`. Every known-red needs BOTH an issue and a reason.

accepted  | 20260920T155254Z | expect=74 | known-red=10 | elsewhere=1

# --- not this suite's to run ------------------------------------------------
# Cross-checked against the test's own `// Runner:` header: a test declares its
# runner, and the manifest agrees, or fast gate 0 fails. #1101 G2 — the Android
# suite ran this `-d linux` host test against the guest, where `test-sshd` is
# unresolvable, so it was a permanent fake red.
elsewhere | desktop_smoke_test.dart | scripts/desktop-smoke.sh

# --- known red, each with the issue that owns it (11) -----------------------
# G7 REAL PRODUCT BUGS (3) — these stay red until the product is fixed. Do NOT
# reclassify one to make a number look better; the baseline attributed them.
known-red | attention_notification_post_test.dart | #1188 | OSC 9 lands inside #851's 1500ms reconnect-replay window, so the attention post is suppressed
known-red | sftp_favorites_test.dart | #948 | regression guard for an open bug: reopening favorites while the cwd IS the favorite renders favorites-empty
known-red | golden_flow_tui_test.dart | #1200 | the gutter long-press-drag produces no Clipboard.setData at all; mechanism undetermined
# G4 STALE (3) — assert the fork's BAKED highlight background, which #1074 removed
# on purpose when the wash became a live widget layer. Behaviour is fine; the
# observation point moved. Re-point at GhosttyWashLayer / DetectionStyleResolver.
known-red | detection_lab_1031_test.dart | #1101 | G4: asserts a baked highlight background that #1074 stopped producing (wash is a live layer now)
known-red | detection_lab_custom_1031_test.dart | #1101 | G4: same pre-#1074 observation point for custom span anchors
known-red | url_bubble_wrap_988_test.dart | #1101 | G4: same pre-#1074 observation point, per-row across a wrap
# G5 STALE (1)
known-red | import_upsert_diversity_test.dart | #1101 | G5: asserts the PEM paste field, but #1121 preselects the profile's attached key so the editor renders the stored-key note
# G6 HARNESS timing (1)
known-red | mermaid_markdown_render_test.dart | #1201 | seeds the fixture before shellReady, and input written at that seam is silently dropped
# G6b DEVICE geometry (2)
known-red | profile_color_picker_1030_test.dart | #1101 | G6b: ensureVisible races the keyboard animation and warnIfMissed:false swallows the miss
known-red | wrap_join_copy_test.dart | #1101 | G6b: anchors the gutter band at 5% of box height, which is viewport row 1 at this device's geometry, so the head row is outside it

